From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GoProSlowYo <68455785+goproslowyo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:25:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] dndcp: Send guest file lists to the host in a Wayland
 session

Send a guest file copy to the host. A file selection is checked first,
before an image or text, because it also advertises a text rendering of
the paths. The backend reads text/uri-list, or
x-special/gnome-copied-files where a selection offers only that. It
parses each entry on its own and skips one that names no local file,
such as a trash: URI, so that the rest of the list still goes to the
host. Lists are compared after parsing, so the same list in another
rendering reads as unchanged.

A path is refused when it is relative, has a . or .. component, or has
no usable last component, which the host names its copy after. Paths
inside the vmblock mount are skipped, because a lookup there blocks
until the main loop lifts the block, and the host has no reason to pull
its own files back. For that the UI now gets the backend's vmblock
control, which a later patch brings up.

The host shows the total size of the files. The paths are sized on a
separate thread, without following symlinks, and the main loop waits for
it only until the request's deadline. A walk still running then is told
to stop, and the list goes to the host with the part of the size that
was counted. At most one walk runs at a time.

The backend now advertises file copy and paste. A host file copy is
pasted from the next patch on.
